        "title": "Digital Fashion and Virtual Dress",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                 DIGITAL FASHION LANDSCAPE                        |\n|                                                                  |\n|  CATEGORIES                                                      |\n|  1. Virtual-only fashion: exists only as digital file/image      |\n|  2. Gaming fashion: skins, cosmetics in game environments        |\n|  3. Digital fashion for social media: photos + video             |\n|  4. AR fashion: overlay on physical body via camera              |\n|  5. NFT fashion: blockchain-ownership of digital garments        |\n|  6. AI-generated fashion: design tool and creative partner       |\n|  7. 3D design tools: CLO, Browzwear (design before sampling)     |\n|                                                                  |\n|  MARKET SIZE                                                     |\n|  Metaverse fashion projections: speculative, hype-era numbers    |\n|  Gaming cosmetics: large proven market, bigger than NFT fashion  |\n|  NFT fashion: peaked 2021-2022; collapsed 2022-2023              |\n|                                                                  |\n|  SUSTAINABILITY CLAIM:                                           |\n|  No physical material; no transportation                         |\n|  Counter: servers have energy cost; demand may complement        |\n|  physical fashion desire, not replace it                         |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
